%I A400774 #31 Nov 13 2026 19:44:01
%S A400774 1,10,21,22,23,24,25,26,27,28,29,31,32,33,34,36,37,38,39,41,42,43,44,
%T A400774 45,47,48,49,51,52,53,54,55,58,59,61,62,63,64,65,66,68,69,71,72,73,74,
%U A400774 75,76,78,79,81,82,83,84,85,86,87,88,89,91,92,93,94,95,96,97,99,101,102,103,104,105,106
%N A400774 Numbers k such that there is no j with 1 <= j < k such that the product of digits of k is the sum of the product of digits of j and the product of digits of k-j.
%C A400774 Numbers k such that A401802(k) = 0.
%C A400774 No term > 109 contains the digit 0.
%C A400774 With the exception of the terms 101, 102, ..., 109, all digits except possibly the last are in nondecreasing order, i.e. A059995(a(n)) is in A009994 unless 68 <= n <= 76.
%C A400774 For terms > 109, two adjacent digits other than the last two must have a product >= 10 and can't be 34, 36, 44, 46, or 66.
%C A400774 Contains A002282(n) and A002283(n) for n >= 2.
%H A400774 Robert Israel, <a href="/A400774/b400774.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2000</a>
%e A400774 a(5) = 23 is a term because A007954(23) = 6 and for j from 1 to 22, A007954(j) + A007954(23-j) is in {3, 4, 5, 13} but is never 6.
%e A400774 35 is not a term because A007954(35) = 15 = 6 + 9 = A007954(16) + A007954(19).
%p A400774 pd:= n -> convert(convert(n,base,10),`*`):
%p A400774 filter:= proc(n) local t;
%p A400774   t:= pd(n);
%p A400774   not ormap(k -> pd(k) + pd(n-k) = t, [$1..n/2])
%p A400774 end proc:
%p A400774 select(filter, [$1..200]);
%t A400774 okQ[k_]:=!MemberQ[Times@@@IntegerDigits[k-Range[k-1]]+Times@@@IntegerDigits[Range[k-1]],Times@@IntegerDigits[k]];Select[Range[106],okQ] (* _James C. McMahon_, Nov 13 2026 *)
%Y A400774 Cf. A002282, A002283, A007954, A009994, A059995, A401802, A401862, A401881.
%K A400774 nonn,base,new
%O A400774 1,2
%A A400774 _Robert Israel_, Nov 04 2026
